# The open standard for agent-ready project documentation

One format. Every AI coding agent. Define your project context once — all major AI coding agents understand it automatically.

[Read the Spec](/spec){primary}
[Quick Start](/getting-started)
::

::section[bg=dark]
## 5 AI tools. 5 config formats. 0 standards.

Every AI coding agent invented its own way to read project context. Your team maintains duplicate files that drift out of sync.

::before-after[transition="replaced by"]
### Before
- Claude Code | CLAUDE.md
- Codex CLI | AGENTS.md
- Cursor | .cursorrules
- GitHub Copilot | .github/copilot-instructions.md
- Windsurf | .windsurfrules

### After
- SurfContext | CONTEXT.surf + .context/ + surfcontext.json
::
::

::section
## How it works

Three files. Universal compatibility. Zero lock-in.

::steps
### Write your context {time="5 min"}
Create `CONTEXT.surf` and a `.context/` directory with your agent definitions and knowledge docs. SurfDoc (`.surf`) is the native format; Markdown stays a supported alias.

### Target platforms {time="2 min"}
Add `surfcontext.json` to declare which AI platforms to generate config files for.

### AI auto-discovers {time="0 min"}
Open your project in any supported AI tool. It reads your context automatically — no copy-paste, no per-tool config.
::
::

::section[bg=dark]
## Platform compatibility

SurfContext generates the right config file for each platform from a single source of truth.

::comparison[highlight="Status"]
| Generated File | Status |
|---------------|--------|
| CLAUDE.md | yes |
| AGENTS.md | yes |
| .cursorrules | yes |
| .github/copilot-instructions.md | yes |
| .windsurfrules | yes |
::
::

::section
